WEBVTT

00:00.234 --> 00:01.766
&lt;i>Previously on&lt;/i>
Two and a Half Men...

00:01.791 --> 00:03.277
I am determined to find

00:03.377 --> 00:04.654
someone who wants
to be with me

00:04.655 --> 00:06.898
for who I am, not what I have.

00:07.144 --> 00:08.993
My point is you can be whoever
you want to be.

00:09.281 --> 00:10.396
I can help you out with that.

00:10.398 --> 00:12.682
I appreciate it... Kate.

00:12.684 --> 00:13.733
Sam Wilson.

00:13.735 --> 00:15.685
Maybe you could crash here.

00:15.687 --> 00:16.736
Have you really
thought this through?

00:16.738 --> 00:19.038
I got to see
where this goes with Kate.

00:19.040 --> 00:20.290
I think it is great

00:20.292 --> 00:22.375
that you're working on
your computer stuff,

00:22.377 --> 00:24.026
but we need help now.

00:24.028 --> 00:25.044
Say no more.

00:25.046 --> 00:27.246
I'll start looking
for a job.

00:31.919 --> 00:33.202
Hey.

00:33.204 --> 00:36.472
Oh, look who finally
decided to show up.

00:36.474 --> 00:38.374
Uh, yeah, I got
stuck in traffic.

00:38.376 --> 00:39.475
Traffic, pfft.

00:39.477 --> 00:42.145
You were with &lt;i>her,&lt;/i>
weren't you?

00:42.147 --> 00:44.514
Really, Alan?

00:44.516 --> 00:46.349
Well, I don't mean to sound
like a broken record,

00:46.351 --> 00:47.567
but you're never
home anymore.

00:47.569 --> 00:49.102
I was just there
the other night.

00:49.104 --> 00:50.403
And all you did
was watch the game

00:50.405 --> 00:52.438
and fall asleep.
Remember how we used

00:52.440 --> 00:54.724
to stay up all night
and just talk?

00:54.726 --> 00:57.493
Okay, you know, fine,
we can talk now.

00:57.495 --> 00:58.444
What's on your mind?

00:58.446 --> 00:59.895
Nothing. I'm fine.

00:59.897 --> 01:03.399
(sighs) I'm not
a mind reader, Alan.

01:03.401 --> 01:06.336
Well, not that
you care, but...

01:06.338 --> 01:08.121
I'm rattling around
in that big house

01:08.123 --> 01:09.122
all by myself.

01:09.124 --> 01:12.458
I miss you.
There, I said it.

01:12.460 --> 01:13.710
I miss you, too.

01:13.712 --> 01:15.911
Well, you got a funny
way of showing it.

01:15.913 --> 01:18.348
You do understand I have
a girlfriend, right?

01:18.350 --> 01:19.248
So do I.

01:19.250 --> 01:21.184
A-Another peach
mojito, please.

01:21.186 --> 01:23.386
What are you drinking?
It's on me.

01:23.388 --> 01:24.887
And by "on me,"
I mean the money

01:24.889 --> 01:26.305
you left me to
pay the bills,

01:26.307 --> 01:27.857
which, incidentally,
I used for other stuff,

01:27.859 --> 01:29.759
so I'll need money
to pay the bills.

01:31.979 --> 01:33.696
I'll have
a ginger ale, please.

01:33.698 --> 01:34.981
Ginger ale?

01:34.983 --> 01:36.983
Yeah, my stomach's
been bothering me.

01:36.985 --> 01:38.768
I haven't really been
feeling myself lately.

01:38.770 --> 01:39.935
Which self would
that be?

01:39.937 --> 01:41.604
Walden Schmidt
or Sam Wilson?

01:41.606 --> 01:44.490
Sam Wilson has
a lot of stress.

01:44.492 --> 01:45.875
Thank you.

01:45.877 --> 01:46.959
Money's tight.

01:46.961 --> 01:49.111
You'd be surprised
what that does to a guy.

01:49.113 --> 01:50.663
Please, I've been so
desperate for money,

01:50.665 --> 01:52.331
I've climbed into
fountains at night

01:52.333 --> 01:54.967
and stolen the
wishes of children.

01:54.969 --> 01:56.636
So you get it.

01:56.638 --> 01:57.920
What I don't get
is why you don't

01:57.922 --> 01:59.806
resolve the stress and just
tell Kate the truth.

01:59.808 --> 02:01.090
(scoffs)
That's not gonna happen.

02:01.092 --> 02:02.141
Why not?
I don't know,

02:02.143 --> 02:03.793
everything's
going so great,

02:03.795 --> 02:05.311
I don't want
to screw it up.

02:05.313 --> 02:08.181
Oh, that's not good.

02:09.049 --> 02:11.722
♪ Men, men, men, men,
manly men, men, men ♪

02:11.747 --> 02:12.338
♪ Ah...
♪ Men.

02:12.339 --> 02:16.339
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 10x12 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Welcome to Alancrest&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on January 3, 2013

02:16.340 --> 02:20.340
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

02:21.410 --> 02:22.860
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

02:23.660 --> 02:25.744
I don't know whether this is
beef or chicken,

02:25.746 --> 02:27.996
but it's definitely
worth 79 cents.

02:31.383 --> 02:32.667
What's the matter?

02:32.669 --> 02:36.204
My life has been
a complete waste of time.

02:36.206 --> 02:38.923
Otherwise, I'm terrific.

02:38.925 --> 02:40.291
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

02:40.293 --> 02:42.577
Wait, is this...
is this one of

02:42.579 --> 02:43.828
the dresses you made?
Mm-hmm.

02:43.830 --> 02:45.513
Why are you throwing it away?

02:45.515 --> 02:48.433
Because, apparently...
my stuff's not good enough

02:48.435 --> 02:51.019
to get a job
that pays nothing.

02:51.021 --> 02:53.021
You didn't get the internship?

02:53.023 --> 02:56.474
Nope. Rejected by the guy
who assists the guy

02:56.476 --> 02:59.611
who assists the guy
who designs Snooki's

02:59.613 --> 03:03.031
signature line
of baby thongs.

03:03.033 --> 03:05.516
Okay, don't worry,
you're gonna get next one.

03:05.518 --> 03:08.119
There is no next one.

03:08.121 --> 03:09.988
I mean, obviously

03:09.990 --> 03:12.190
I don't have what it takes
to be a fashion designer.

03:12.192 --> 03:14.626
And at a certain point,
I just have to bite the bullet

03:14.628 --> 03:16.377
and admit it is not happening.

03:16.379 --> 03:18.079
But you're not at that point.

03:18.081 --> 03:19.547
Three words:

03:19.549 --> 03:21.032
Snooki's...

03:21.034 --> 03:22.366
baby...

03:22.368 --> 03:24.419
thongs!

03:24.421 --> 03:26.537
I think your designs are great.

03:26.539 --> 03:28.923
You have to say that;
I have sex with you.

03:30.192 --> 03:31.559
True.

03:31.561 --> 03:35.730
But if I was a woman,
I would totally wear this dress.

03:36.682 --> 03:38.049
Hell, three shots of tequila

03:38.051 --> 03:39.567
and I would wear this dress.

03:40.385 --> 03:42.487
And I would work it!
(grunts)

03:42.489 --> 03:45.223
Okay, don't make me laugh
when I'm trying to cry.

03:45.225 --> 03:47.025
Too late, because
I am fierce.

03:47.027 --> 03:50.278
(humming dance music)
(laughing)

03:52.164 --> 03:53.564
I love you, Sam.

03:53.566 --> 03:56.401
Uh, you have to say that;
I have sex with you.

03:56.403 --> 03:58.753
Okay, the real test is,

03:58.755 --> 04:01.239
will you have sex with me
wearing that dress?

04:01.241 --> 04:04.926
You get the tequila,
I'll go put on some heels.

04:08.631 --> 04:10.765
Lightly salted,
just the way you like.

04:10.767 --> 04:12.550
Mm, thanks.
(chuckles)

04:12.552 --> 04:14.469
Who could've seen
this coming?

04:14.471 --> 04:15.436
Right.

04:15.438 --> 04:17.222
We end up with the house.
(chuckles)

04:17.224 --> 04:19.691
Unbelievable.

04:19.693 --> 04:21.226
You know how
I used to say

04:21.228 --> 04:23.194
you'd have to pay me
to hang out with you?

04:23.196 --> 04:24.195
Yeah.

04:24.197 --> 04:26.364
Here we are!

04:27.233 --> 04:28.483
WALDEN:
Hey, guys.

04:28.485 --> 04:29.600
Mm.
!

04:29.602 --> 04:31.569
Oh, Look who it is.
Sam Wilson.

04:31.571 --> 04:32.704
Hey, Alan,

04:32.706 --> 04:34.122
can I, can I talk to you
for a second?

04:34.124 --> 04:35.106
Oh, sure.

04:35.108 --> 04:37.408
The principal wants to see me.
Mm.

04:38.711 --> 04:41.462
Oh, uh, Berta,
I brought some laundry by.

04:41.464 --> 04:42.797
Uh, do you mind?

04:42.799 --> 04:45.500
It's your machine.
Knock yourself out.

04:49.004 --> 04:50.772
So, what's up?

04:50.774 --> 04:53.641
I'm transferring $100,000
into your bank account.

04:53.643 --> 04:56.561
(gasps):
A hundred... thousand...

04:56.563 --> 04:57.845
Catch me, Lord.

04:57.847 --> 04:58.897
(panting)

04:58.899 --> 04:59.981
Uh-oh, uh-oh.

04:59.983 --> 05:01.399
I-I think I need
to sit down.

05:01.401 --> 05:02.750
Yeah, yeah.
I...

05:02.752 --> 05:04.802
I-I could swear
that I heard you say

05:04.804 --> 05:06.821
you were gonna put
$100,000 into my account.

05:06.823 --> 05:07.855
I am.

05:07.857 --> 05:10.024
There it goes again.

05:10.026 --> 05:12.110
It's-it's like the teacups
at Disneyland.

05:12.112 --> 05:14.746
How can I ever thank you?

05:14.748 --> 05:16.647
The money's not for you,
it's for Kate.

05:16.649 --> 05:18.499
Next time, lead with that.

05:18.501 --> 05:20.501
I want you to invest
in her fashion designs.

05:20.503 --> 05:22.503
What?
She's really talented,

05:22.505 --> 05:24.155
but nobody will
give her a shot.

05:24.157 --> 05:25.823
Are you sure she's talented?

05:25.825 --> 05:27.491
It isn't just
boom-shaka-laka-laka,

05:27.493 --> 05:29.210
boom-shaka-laka-laka?

05:30.195 --> 05:32.496
I'm about to give you
a boom-shaka-laka.

05:33.999 --> 05:36.768
No, $100,000 will help
her start her company.

05:36.770 --> 05:38.686
So give it to her.
I can't.

05:38.688 --> 05:40.188
I'm Sam Wilson.
I'm broke.

05:40.190 --> 05:42.340
But you can,
because you're

05:42.342 --> 05:44.142
Alan Harper,
billionaire.

05:44.144 --> 05:46.344
Oh...

05:48.197 --> 05:50.982
Fashion's kind of risky.

05:52.334 --> 05:54.485
And Alan Harper did not
become a billionaire

05:54.487 --> 05:56.504
by taking unnecessary risks.

05:56.506 --> 05:59.857
You are taking an
unnecessary risk right now.

05:59.859 --> 06:02.627
No, I-I'm just saying that I'd
rather put my money into gold,

06:02.629 --> 06:04.078
or maybe start a vineyard.

06:04.080 --> 06:05.529
Alancrest.

06:05.531 --> 06:08.883
You know, fine, when
you make $100,000--

06:08.885 --> 06:10.585
I don't even have
to finish that.

06:10.587 --> 06:14.422
I-I want &lt;i>my&lt;/i> money
invested in Kate.

06:14.424 --> 06:16.507
Okay, no problem.

06:16.509 --> 06:19.477
But I'll have to see
some of her sketches first.

06:19.479 --> 06:19.839
Alan.

06:19.864 --> 06:21.790
What? You want this to be
believable, don't you?

06:22.265 --> 06:23.531
Okay, fine.

06:23.533 --> 06:24.899
Have us over
tomorrow night.

06:24.901 --> 06:26.601
Ooh, kind of short notice.

06:26.603 --> 06:27.935
Alan!

06:27.937 --> 06:29.237
Can't we do this at your house?

06:29.239 --> 06:32.440
This is my house!

06:35.327 --> 06:39.397
Awfully rude for a guy
who wants my money.

06:50.626 --> 06:53.945
It's like you've never
washed a dish in your life.

06:53.947 --> 06:56.014
What are you
talking about?

06:56.016 --> 06:58.466
There's still SpaghettiOs
on this plate.

06:58.468 --> 07:00.184
(chuckles)

07:00.186 --> 07:02.553
Well, you're the one
that wanted to be all fancy

07:02.555 --> 07:05.440
and said we couldn't eat them
straight out of the can.

07:06.358 --> 07:07.475
Ugh.

07:07.477 --> 07:10.528
Oh, speaking of fancy,
I saw Alan today.

07:10.530 --> 07:12.230
Ew.

07:12.232 --> 07:15.116
It was actually a really
interesting conversation.

07:15.118 --> 07:17.535
He's looking for some
new investments.

07:17.537 --> 07:20.788
He should go and buy himself
a better personality.

07:20.790 --> 07:22.657
Nobody's that rich.

07:22.659 --> 07:25.743
Uh, but I did tell him
that you're trying to start

07:25.745 --> 07:27.278
your own fashion company.

07:27.280 --> 07:28.946
Oh, Sam, you didn't.

07:28.948 --> 07:30.581
Oh, but I did.

07:31.617 --> 07:33.301
Well, he's in a position
to help you.

07:33.303 --> 07:34.752
I don't want his help.

07:34.754 --> 07:36.504
Unless I'm gonna start
a line called

07:36.506 --> 07:38.840
House of Douche.

07:38.842 --> 07:40.141
Don't be ridiculous.

07:40.143 --> 07:42.460
I'm sure that name's
already taken.

07:42.462 --> 07:45.480
Hey, he could be the answer
to all your problems.

07:45.482 --> 07:46.797
Oh, I don't know.

07:46.799 --> 07:48.015
Before you say no,

07:48.017 --> 07:49.684
he invited us over
tomorrow night

07:49.686 --> 07:51.686
so you can show him
your designs.

07:52.604 --> 07:55.189
Really think he'd invest in me?

07:55.191 --> 07:56.858
He'd have to be an idiot not to.

07:56.860 --> 07:58.493
But he is an idiot.

07:58.495 --> 08:01.145
True.

08:02.197 --> 08:03.614
Give it a chance?

08:03.616 --> 08:04.982
All right.

08:04.984 --> 08:06.167
I'll do it.

08:06.169 --> 08:08.703
Great. Oh, did I mention
that if you take his money,

08:08.705 --> 08:10.204
you have to
sleep with him?

08:10.206 --> 08:12.256
(gags)

08:12.258 --> 08:14.675
I'm kidding;
I'll totally do him.

08:14.677 --> 08:15.877
(gags)

08:15.879 --> 08:17.945
(laughs)

08:19.848 --> 08:22.016
(doorbell rings)

08:25.003 --> 08:26.637
Ah! Sam, Kate.

08:26.639 --> 08:28.172
Welcome to Alancrest.

08:28.174 --> 08:30.558
W-Why are you
wearing pajamas?

08:30.560 --> 08:32.193
I'm rich. I can.

08:32.195 --> 08:34.729
Mm. You have
a beautiful home.

08:34.731 --> 08:36.514
It'll work
until my castle's finished.

08:36.516 --> 08:39.033
&lt;i>Entrez-vous.&lt;/i>

08:39.035 --> 08:41.536
Uh, that's French for
"enter, you."

08:41.538 --> 08:43.004
Oh, look,

08:43.006 --> 08:44.739
my panoramic ocean view.
(laughs)

08:44.741 --> 08:47.074
You can follow my
seagulls on Twitter.

08:48.210 --> 08:50.244
Hashtag, "Gulls gone wild."

08:51.497 --> 08:52.696
Oh, ah, delightful!

08:52.698 --> 08:55.082
Thank you, Berta.
That will be all.

08:55.084 --> 08:57.218
Damn right it will!

08:57.220 --> 08:59.870
(laughs) She's been
with the family for years.

08:59.872 --> 09:01.589
They say you're not really rich

09:01.591 --> 09:03.707
until you have servants
who hate you.

09:03.709 --> 09:06.811
Uh, Alan, Kate brought
her portfolio to show you.

09:06.813 --> 09:08.095
Oh, yes!

09:08.097 --> 09:09.647
Kate, please
take a seat.

09:09.649 --> 09:11.098
(laughs)
Take my breath away!

09:11.100 --> 09:13.267
Oh, I'd love to.

09:13.269 --> 09:16.404
I made some new sketches
just for you.

09:16.406 --> 09:18.239
Uh, yeah, she's been
working really hard on them.

09:18.241 --> 09:20.274
I-I think you're really
gonna like what you see.

09:20.276 --> 09:21.242
(laughs)
No offense, Sam,

09:21.244 --> 09:23.444
but look at the
way &lt;i>you&lt;/i> dress.

09:24.329 --> 09:26.030
Mm.

09:26.032 --> 09:27.331
All right.

09:27.333 --> 09:29.450
Oh, it's-it's nice.

09:29.452 --> 09:31.169
No, I-I like
what you did here.

09:31.171 --> 09:32.236
Thank you.

09:33.205 --> 09:35.006
Uh, cap sleeves are
last season, but,

09:35.008 --> 09:37.241
you know, okay.
(laughs)

09:38.076 --> 09:39.510
Oh, you know,
I'm kind of done

09:39.512 --> 09:41.592
with rompers, but I understand
what you're going for.

09:42.581 --> 09:43.848
Oh, oh.

09:43.850 --> 09:45.183
Velvet.
(chuckles)

09:45.185 --> 09:46.601
(singsong):
Kind of whorish.

09:46.603 --> 09:49.136
Excuse me?
WALDEN: Okay.

09:49.138 --> 09:51.973
You know what, uh, Kate,
why don't you run out to the car

09:51.975 --> 09:53.224
and grab some of your samples.

09:53.226 --> 09:55.393
I think Alan would
love to see them.

09:55.395 --> 09:56.944
Yeah, sure.

09:56.946 --> 09:59.564
Just hope
they're not too whorish.

09:59.566 --> 10:00.598
Yeah.

10:00.600 --> 10:02.733
Let's leave that
to Lady Gaga.

10:04.786 --> 10:06.404
Ow!

10:07.539 --> 10:09.457
What the hell
is the matter with you?

10:09.459 --> 10:11.876
Me? She's the one
who paired an empire waist

10:11.878 --> 10:13.961
with a Peter Pan collar!

10:13.963 --> 10:18.883
You're supposed to be a simple
rich guy, not a gay Bruce Wayne.

10:18.885 --> 10:21.886
Hey, hey, you have
your character, I have mine.

10:21.888 --> 10:24.639
Well, your character is a
festering heap of human waste!

10:24.641 --> 10:27.508
I think we both know, if I had
money, I'd be the biggest

10:27.510 --> 10:30.928
festering heap of human waste
that ever lived!

10:30.930 --> 10:33.814
All you have to do is tell her
that you want to invest

10:33.816 --> 10:35.600
and give her my $100,000.

10:35.602 --> 10:38.903
Well, fine,
but velvet is whorish.

10:38.905 --> 10:40.521
Okay, here we are.

10:40.523 --> 10:43.190
Uh, let's see.

10:43.192 --> 10:45.309
This is a cute, little shift

10:45.311 --> 10:47.278
that goes from
day to night.

10:47.280 --> 10:49.280
I love them all!
What?

10:49.282 --> 10:50.665
You-you haven't even seen them.

10:50.667 --> 10:53.000
I've seen all I
need to see, Kate.

10:53.002 --> 10:55.336
I want to invest in
your line of clothing.

10:55.338 --> 10:56.120
Really?

10:56.122 --> 10:57.121
Yes! Now tell me,

10:57.123 --> 10:58.172
what's our
business plan?

10:58.174 --> 10:59.674
Well, it depends.
If I had enough money,

10:59.676 --> 11:01.509
I'd put a show together for
Fashion Week in New York.

11:01.511 --> 11:02.593
That way, I'd be able to...

11:02.595 --> 11:05.329
Sounds great. Pack
your bags for New York,

11:05.331 --> 11:10.000
because I'm gonna write
you a check for $50,000.

11:10.002 --> 11:12.019
KATE and WALDEN:
What?!

11:12.021 --> 11:13.387
Sam, did you hear that?

11:13.389 --> 11:14.805
Uh, yeah, I did.

11:14.807 --> 11:16.340
What's the-- $50,000?

11:16.342 --> 11:17.692
I-I know it's a lot.

11:17.694 --> 11:20.344
But I believe in her, and
I want to take a chance.

11:20.346 --> 11:21.612
WALDEN:
Uh, well,

11:21.614 --> 11:23.314
if you really believe
in her, maybe you'd...

11:23.316 --> 11:25.232
maybe you'd like to invest
a little bit more.

11:25.234 --> 11:25.849
Sam.

11:25.851 --> 11:26.984
No, no, no.

11:26.986 --> 11:29.120
He's right.

11:29.122 --> 11:31.572
I'm gonna hate
myself for this.

11:31.574 --> 11:33.958
But what the heck.

11:33.960 --> 11:37.545
$60,000.

11:37.547 --> 11:40.214
(laughing)

11:44.035 --> 11:47.972
I can't believe Alan
gave me $100,000.

11:47.974 --> 11:51.592
I can't believe
it took him two hours to do it.

11:51.594 --> 11:53.928
Thank you.

11:53.930 --> 11:56.380
What are you thanking me for?

11:56.382 --> 11:59.433
Because I know none of this
would've happened without you.

11:59.435 --> 12:01.435
I just introduced you.

12:01.437 --> 12:03.821
Your whorish velvet
did the rest.

12:03.823 --> 12:06.741
(laughs)

12:06.743 --> 12:08.743
You are the sweetest...

12:08.745 --> 12:11.412
most generous...

12:11.414 --> 12:13.781
open, giving...

12:13.783 --> 12:16.534
